# data file for fldtk fluid (Fast Light User Interface Designer)
version 1.0000
comment {The interactive editor's widget palette ("Tools" window).

Ported from FLTK's fluid/panels/function_panel.fl -- only the
`make_widgetbin()` window (`widgetbin_panel`, renamed `widgetBinPanel`
here for this project's own camelCase convention), but now the FULL
window: all 8 group boxes, all 57 buttons, every one at FLTK's own
literal `xywh` slot. Window size (600x102) is FLTK's own too.

Every button FLTK has gets a slot here, whether or not this port
can act on it yet -- a deliberate choice, not an oversight: omitting
anything not yet wired up would mean re-deriving FLTK's own geometry a
second time later
-- rereading `panels/function_panel.fl`, re-finding every xywh, re-
grouping -- pure wasted work when the data is sitting right here
already. So: every slot exists, permanently, and only a button's
*class* (`BinButton` vs plain `Button`) changes as this port's
`fluid.factory`/`fluid.instantiate` registries grow.

Two kinds of button, distinguished by whether the widget type it names
is registered in both `fluid.factory` (Node-parsing side) and
`fluid.instantiate` (live-widget side) today:

- **Real** (`class \{BinButton\}`, real `tooltip`, `setup \{o.typeName
  ("X");\}`, `callback binButtonCb`) -- click to add at a default
  position, or drag onto the canvas to drop at the exact release
  point via real XDND. See `fluid/panels/BinButton.d`'s own doc
  comment for the click-vs-drag mechanism. The Code group's own 9
  buttons are "real" in this same sense but wired to a
  second delegate, `callback codeButtonCb` -- they still reuse
  `BinButton` for its `typeName()` storage, but a `Function`/`decl`/
  `comment`/... node is never a live canvas widget, so only the click
  path (`gui_main.d`'s `addNode()`, the non-widget counterpart of
  `addWidget()`) actually does anything; dragging one onto the canvas
  is a harmless no-op (matches FLTK's own real split -- these 9
  used a plain click-only `type_make_cb` there too, never `Bin_Button`'s
  drag machinery).
- **Placeholder** (plain `Button`, real `tooltip` with a "(not yet
  implemented)" suffix, `deactivate`, no `class`/`callback` -- but a
  real `setup \{o.image(pixmapFor("X"));\}` icon too,
  see below) -- present at the exact FLTK position so the grid
  never needs re-deriving, but genuinely inert: a deactivated widget
  never receives push/drag events at all (matches this port's own
  established `deactivate()` semantics), so there's no risk of it
  reaching `createNode()`/`addWidget()` with a type name neither
  registry actually knows yet (`fluid.factory.createNode()` throws on
  an unknown type name -- a placeholder must never be able to trigger
  that). **To promote a placeholder to real** once its type is
  registered: swap its block for the "Real" shape above (`class`,
  `o.typeName(...)` alongside the existing `o.image(...)` call,
  `callback`, dropping `deactivate` and the tooltip suffix) -- a small,
  mechanical edit, not a re-port. No FLTK re-reading needed; the
  position/tooltip/icon are already here.

Placeholder reasons, by category -- only two categories have any left:
Table is real but, matching FLTK's own `Table_Node`'s much bigger
`add_child()`/`move_child()` override machinery, this port's own Table
support is leaf-only for now -- no live widget-in-cell children yet,
see its own tooltip. The Code group (all 9) needed a new, non-widget-shaped insertion path
(`gui_main.d`'s `addNode()`) and a node-browser fix (`NodeBrowser.
build()` widened from a single window root to the whole `projectRoots_`
forest -- otherwise a newly-added top-level `Function`/`decl` would
have had nowhere to render in the project tree at all), not just a
registry entry -- see this file's own `codeButtonCb` note above):
- **Menus group**: `checkmenuitem`/`submenu`/`radiomenuitem` (3 of the
  original 4) -- a different node kind (`MenuItemNode`, a menu owner's
  child, not a general canvas widget) that `addWidget()`'s current
  insertion path can't target at all, a real, separate mechanism gap
  even once the node kind itself is technically parseable.
  `Fl_Input_Choice`/`Fl_Menu_Bar` are real --
  both are concrete subclasses of FLTK's abstract
  `Menu_Manager_Node`, the same "widget that owns a menu, can have
  `MenuItem` children" role `Menu_Button`/`Choice` (already real) fill,
  which this port's own `MenuOwnerNode` already covers generically;
  registering the two remaining concrete types (`fluid.factory`/
  `fluid.instantiate`) needed no new mechanism at all, just two more
  registry entries -- see `PORTING.md`'s `fluid/nodes/` row for the
  full writeup. All 4 of the menu-item family are real in the `&New`
  menu (`fluid.factory` registers
  `"Submenu"`/`"CheckMenuItem"`/`"RadioMenuItem"`/`"MenuItem"`, see
  `fluid.menu_item_node`'s own doc comment for why `CheckMenuItem`/
  `RadioMenuItem` are plain `MenuItemNode`s while `Submenu` gets a real
  `SubmenuNode` subclass), but these 4 bin buttons specifically are
  still placeholders -- promoting them needs the same `codeButtonCb`-
  style click-only wiring `Fl_Window`'s own promotion got below.

`Fl_Window` is promoted to real --
neither of the two existing callback kinds above fit it exactly, so it
gets a **third**: still `class \{BinButton\}`/`callback binButtonCb`
(the same delegate every ordinary widget button uses), but
`binButtonCb`'s own body (`gui_main.d`) now special-cases
`typeName() == "Window"` to call a dedicated `createWindowNode()`
instead of the generic `addWidget()` every other real button falls
through to -- ported from FLTK's own `Window_Node::make()`: walks
up from the current selection for a `FunctionNode` ancestor and nests
the new window there, or shows `fl_message()`'s real "Please select a
function" if none exists, rather than `addWidget()`'s generic
"current selection or project root" fallback (which would silently
create a window with no enclosing function, something `code_writer.d`
has no shape for). Still no nested-window *canvas rendering* --
`instantiate.d`'s `instantiateChild()` still skips `WindowNode`s, so a
newly-created window shows up in the project tree and generates real
code, just isn't drawn live -- that structural gap is unchanged, only
node *creation* is new here. Dragging this button onto the canvas
still isn't a real drop target either (`instantiateChild()`'s guard
makes it a harmless no-op rather than a crash, but there's genuinely
nowhere useful for the drop to land).

Real icons, for real buttons *and*
placeholders alike -- every button gets its own 16x16 FLTK icon
via `fluid.pixmaps.pixmapFor()`, the type-name-keyed lookup table
backed by FLTK's own real `fluid/pixmaps/*.xpm` assets,
mechanically transliterated (see that module's own top comment). A
real button's `setup \{\}` calls `o.image(pixmapFor("X"))` right after
`o.typeName("X")`, matching FLTK's own `o->image(pixmap_for(
"Fl_X"))` one-for-one in spirit (the literal string differs since this
dialect's own `typeName()` values are short aliases, not FLTK's
`Fl_`-prefixed names -- `pixmapFor()` resolves both forms, see its own
doc comment). A placeholder has no `typeName()` to read (it's a plain
`Button`, never a `BinButton`), so its own `setup \{\}` passes
`pixmapFor()` the correct FLTK key directly, by hand, and still stays
`deactivate`d: every
one of the 62 ported icons can be visually checked for correctness
even for a type this port doesn't act on yet, without these
buttons becoming functional.
}
